Modifications by Provable Games, based on upstream commit
3d75aee4b3f43cbd932265e7d60201fd5b770397:

  - Removed the GUI panel and <webaudio-tinysynth> custom element;
    retained the JavaScript API and CommonJS/AMD/global exports.
  - Kept fractional MIDI tempo; added loopEnd/setLoopEnd() for loop
    boundaries and getPlayStatus().startTime for visual synchronization.
    Explicit loop boundaries preserve the rest before the first event.
  - Added bounded, validated SMF parsing with coded errors that preserve
    the previous song. Bounded sequencer callbacks, stopped non-advancing
    loops and empty songs, and rebuilt tempo/channel state on seek/replay.
  - Added context/destination/lazy/autoResume constructor options and
    resume()/dispose(). Released voices, nodes and timers; closed only
    synth-owned contexts. Stop/seek cancel drums and queued controllers.
    Rejected realtime sequencing on OfflineAudioContext and handled
    resume promise failures.
  - Validated public arguments and copied timbres before installation;
    ignored malformed raw MIDI, bounded AudioParam values to float32,
    and clamped converted timestamps to the current context time.
    Added cancellable loadMIDIUrl() promises with coded errors and
    protection against stale responses.
  - Corrected note releases during attack to use each operator's reached
    level; retained no-attack operator releases for zero-length notes.
  - Added setSampleWave()/setHarmonicWave() waveform registries and
    optional fixed output-operator filters (fl, ff, fq, fk).
  - Generated reverb/noise buffers with seeded mulberry32 streams;
    added seed and bufferVersion. Metallic noise is generated once per
    context installation on first use or prewarm(); disabled reverb
    does not generate its impulse. Installed built-in timbres once.
  - Updated demos to use the JavaScript API, user-gesture audio startup,
    error reporting and validated timbre editing. Added tests and
    reproducible minified builds; simplified maintained documentation.
  - Regenerated webaudio-tinysynth.min.js and its source map from the
    modified source.

